"notes": "Modified cash basis school district; governmental funds only (School Nutrition and Activities are inside Other Governmental Funds); business_type null. Basic receipts/disbursements from the governmental funds statement Total Governmental Funds column (p4-5). Total column nets the 50,000 interfund transfers (General out, Other funds in) to zero, so transfers_in/out are null; debt proceeds 7,929,416 (Special Building bond proceeds) are listed under other financing sources and are outside printed total receipts. Identity: 3,203,330 + 7,215,735 - 6,680,341 + 7,929,416 = 11,668,140. Detail: General Fund detail combines the General Fund budget schedule receipts (pp9-10, more detailed) with Depreciation and Employee Benefit interest (their transfer-in of 500,000 is eliminated by the reclassification column on p7) so revenue ties to the combining Total 5,973,318; General Fund disbursements use the combining schedule Total column (p8, after reclassifications, includes Depreciation Fund capital outlay 202,124 and the 50,000 transfer) rather than the budget schedule's pre-reclassification lines, which contain a hidden 500,000 transfer to Depreciation; the General Fund budget disbursement schedule (p11) and Depreciation Fund schedule (p12) are therefore not repeated to avoid double counting. Other receiving-fund transfers: School Nutrition +20,000 and Activities +30,000 equal the General Fund's 50,000. Printed zero/blank 2025 lines (e.g. 1980 refund, 4518 IDEA with budget only) omitted. Balance sheet from the Statement of Activities and Net Position (p3), no liabilities. Read pages 1-18 of 18"
